      "description": "Watch Georgia vs Northern Ireland highlights and goals from UEFA Nations League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 25, 2026. Late drama secures crucial points for Northern Ireland On September 25, 2026 , Georgia and Northern Ireland faced off in a tightly contested UEFA Nations League fixture. Both sides approached the encounter with a cautious mindset, aware that a single mistake could alter the course of their campaign in the competition. The penalty heartbreak Midway through the second half, the game reached its boiling point. Following a VAR review, Georgia were awarded a penalty after Daniel Ballard was adjudged to have pulled down Luka Lochoshvili . Khvicha Kvaratskhelia stepped up to break the deadlock, but his effort was expertly saved, denying the hosts a golden opportunity to take command of the match. The missed spot-kick signaled a shift in momentum, as both managers shuffled their packs with multiple tactical substitutions, and frustrations grew, resulting in bookings for several players as the intensity reached a fever pitch. A stunning finish Just as it seemed the points would be shared, Northern Ireland produced a moment of magic deep into stoppage time. In the 90+9th minute, a brilliant cross from Trai Hume found Shea Charles , who lashed a clinical volley into the back of the net. A brief VAR check confirmed the goal stood, silencing the home crowd and handing Northern Ireland a dramatic 1-0 victory in the dying seconds of a physically demanding match."
